<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Malik Raja Faruqi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1399</span> · Also known as Malik Ahmad Raja Faruqi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Malik Raja Faruqi was the founder of the Faruqi dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khandesh">Khandesh</a> in the Tapti valley. Granted lands there by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/firuz-shah-tughluq">Firuz Shah Tughluq</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a>, he became effectively independent around 1382 as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a>'s authority declined. The family claimed descent from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> Umar, and his successors ruled Khandesh from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burhanpur">Burhanpur</a> until the Mughal conquest of 1601.</p></div>
